{"tool_name":"joinet","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"joinet","home":"https://github.com/rauschenberger/joinet","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Multivariate elastic net regression through stacked generalisation","addition_date":"2022-01-15T02:07:39.807713Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:13:04.241778Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:joinet","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"armin.rauschenberger@uni.lu","name":"Armin Rauschenberger","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6498-4801","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Enrico Glaab","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3977-7469"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Regression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3659"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"joinet","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btab576","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Multivariate (multi-target) regression has the potential to outperform univariate (single-target) regression at predicting correlated outcomes, which frequently occur in biomedical and clinical research. Here we implement multivariate lasso and ridge regression using stacked generalization. Results: Our flexible approach leads to predictive and interpretable models in high-dimensional settings, with a single estimate for each input-output effect. In the simulation, we compare the predictive performance of several state-of-the-art methods for multivariate regression. In the application, we use clinical and genomic data to predict multiple motor and non-motor symptoms in Parkinson's disease patients. We conclude that stacked multivariate regression, with our adaptations, is a competitive method for predicting correlated outcomes.","authors":[{"name":"Glaab E."},{"name":"Rauschenberger A."}],"citationCount":